WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:01.612
The Moon's pull.

00:02.312 --> 00:10.498
The Moon pulls on the sea, and the sea rises towards it and on the far side too, so most coasts have two high tides a day.

00:10.948 --> 00:15.229
Over billions of years the same pull has slowed the Earth's spin.

00:15.679 --> 00:21.046
And the Moon is thought to hold the Earth's tilt steady, which keeps the seasons mild.
